Q1. What is Debugging?

Interview Ready Answer

Debugging is the systematic process of identifying, analyzing, isolating, and fixing defects (bugs) in a software application. It is performed after a bug has been detected to determine its root cause and resolve it.

Definition

Debugging is the process of finding and fixing bugs in software.

Purpose

• Identify the root cause of defects.
• Analyze application execution.
• Fix incorrect or unexpected behavior.
• Improve software reliability and stability.

======================================================================

Q2. What is the difference between Testing and Debugging?

Interview Ready Answer

Testing is the process of executing software to identify defects and verify that it behaves as expected. Debugging begins after a defect is found and involves locating the root cause and fixing the issue.

Definition

Testing finds defects.
Debugging fixes defects.

Purpose

• Testing verifies software correctness.
• Debugging removes the cause of failures.

Key Points

• Testing is performed using test cases.
• Debugging is primarily performed by developers.
• Testing identifies defects.
• Debugging analyzes and fixes defects.

======================================================================

Q3. What is a Bug?

Interview Ready Answer

A bug is a defect or flaw in a software application that causes incorrect, unexpected, or unintended behavior. Bugs may result from mistakes in design, logic, implementation, or requirements.

Definition

A bug is a software defect.

Purpose

• Represents an issue that prevents the application from behaving as expected.

Examples

• Incorrect output
• Runtime exception
• Application crash
• Security vulnerability
• Performance issue

======================================================================

Q4. What are the different types of errors in JavaScript?

Interview Ready Answer

The three primary types of errors in JavaScript are:

1. Syntax Errors
2. Runtime Errors
3. Logical Errors

Definition

Syntax Error
• Occurs when the code violates JavaScript syntax rules.
• Prevents the code from executing correctly.

Runtime Error
• Occurs while the program is executing.
• Example: Accessing a property of null or undefined.

Logical Error
• The program executes successfully but produces incorrect results due to incorrect program logic.

Purpose

• Understanding error types helps select the appropriate debugging approach.

======================================================================

Q5. What is a Breakpoint?

Interview Ready Answer

A breakpoint is a debugging marker placed on a specific line of code that pauses program execution when that line is reached. It allows developers to inspect variable values, analyze the call stack, examine the execution flow, and identify the root cause of bugs before continuing execution.

Definition

A breakpoint temporarily pauses program execution during debugging.

Purpose

• Pause execution at a desired location.
• Inspect variables.
• Analyze execution flow.
• Check the call stack.
• Identify the root cause of bugs.

